---
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: zigbee2mqtt-config
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
type: Opaque
stringData:
{#
  Rendered from the Docker role's template, not copied (the configarr precedent) — one config
  source for both planes, so the two cannot drift. The k8s render differs only through
  z2m_mqtt_broker=mosquitto (role default): in-cluster the broker is the Service name, not the
  LAN VIP. A Secret because it embeds the MQTT password and the pinned Zigbee network key.

  An init container installs this into the writable data PVC on every pod start — z2m insists
  on configuration.yaml living beside its data, and re-installing each start is the same
  "Ansible is the source of truth, frontend edits don't survive" contract the Docker role's
  every-deploy re-template enforced.
#}
  configuration.yaml: |
{{ lookup('template', playbook_dir + '/roles/k8s/zigbee2mqtt/templates/config/configuration.yaml.j2') | indent(4, true) }}
